{"_id":"68a7362e8ec3d8323af1c48d","nodeId":"274uk28wzxn6EKWQzLpHs","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# Modules\n\nModules refer to a file containing Python statements and definitions. A file containing Python code, for example: `example.py`, is called a module, and its module name would be example. We use modules to break down large programs into small manageable and organized files. Furthermore, modules provide reusability of code.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Python Modules","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/modules.html","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae37e"},{"type":"article","title":"Modules in Python","url":"https://www.programiz.com/python-programming/modules","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae37f"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/274uk28wzxn6EKWQzLpHs.md"}